# Coding Standards

## Core Philosophy

Prioritize simplicity, scalability, readability, maintainability, performance, and premium UX. Avoid overengineering, unnecessary abstractions, bloated dependencies, deeply nested logic, and massive components.

## Tech Stack

- Next.js 16 App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Framer Motion, Zustand
- Supabase + PostgreSQL

## Components

- Single responsibility; reusable and modular
- No mixed UI + business logic; split when complexity grows

## Naming

| Kind | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| Components | PascalCase | `WeddingHero.tsx` |
| Hooks | `use` + camelCase | `useWeddingData.ts` |
| Utils | kebab-case | `generate-slug.ts` |
| Routes | lowercase kebab | `/dashboard/create-invite`, `/w/rahul-weds-ananya` |

## Folder Structure

```
/app  /components  /features  /templates  /hooks  /lib  /services  /store  /types  /utils
```

Actual project uses `src/` with the same logical layout.

## State

- Zustand for editor, UI, preview state
- Separate persisted data from temporary UI state
- Avoid unnecessary global state, excessive Context, prop drilling

## Styling

- Tailwind consistently; no inline styles or random spacing
- Reuse design tokens and spacing scale

## Responsive

- Mobile-first; test small Android, iPhone, tablet
- No fixed widths, hover-only interactions, desktop-only layouts

## Performance

- Lazy-load images; optimize media; minimize rerenders; dynamic imports when needed
- Reduce client JS; avoid large bundles and heavy animations

## Templates

- Presentation-only; shared `WeddingData` schema; no direct DB access or business logic

## Database (MVP)

- Single `invitations` row with `content` JSONB mapped to `WeddingData` (see project-context)
- Do not normalize into many tables for MVP autosave

## Data Fetching

- Prefer server components, server actions, minimal payloads
- Avoid duplicate client fetches and over-fetching

## Forms

- React Hook Form + Zod; validate client and server; don't duplicate validation logic

## Error Handling

- Always handle loading, empty, and error states
- Never silently fail or expose raw backend errors

## Images

- Compression, resizing, lazy loading, WebP, CDN; never render raw large uploads

## SEO (public pages)

- Dynamic metadata, OpenGraph, WhatsApp previews, clean slugs (`/w/rahul-weds-ananya`)

## Imports (order)

1. external 2. internal 3. components 4. styles 5. types

## Dependencies

- Check bundle size and maintenance before adding packages

## Security

- Never expose API secrets, service role keys, payment secrets
- Validate permissions; use env vars correctly

## Testing (MVP)

- Manual + responsive testing on critical flows: auth, uploads, payment, publishing, public render

## Priority

1. UX 2. mobile 3. performance 4. maintainability 5. simplicity
